WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:01.490
- And whenever I fly to the States,

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:02.323
I've got a place there,

00:00:02.323 --> 00:00:03.910
but I'm always working, right?

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:06.110
So, someone else is playing, all right,

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:08.510
so I go first class BA.

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:09.440
It doesn't get any better.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:10.670
Even if I was paying for my own way,

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:11.810
I'd still go for first class.

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:14.770
But, Jane would probably be in coach.

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:16.320
(audience laughing)

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.896
It's 10 grand a pop. She's...

00:00:17.896 --> 00:00:20.990
That new Planet of the Apes
movies on, she'd love that.

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:24.689
(audience laughing)

00:00:24.689 --> 00:00:26.577
Alright, but when someone
else is paying, I say,

00:00:26.577 --> 00:00:28.150
"Jane, get up here with me."

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:29.109
Right?

00:00:29.109 --> 00:00:29.942
(audience laughing)

00:00:29.942 --> 00:00:32.790
Front two seats, they board us early.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:35.520
We're on the plane about 15
minutes before anyone else is,

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:37.460
oh my God, they bring round these snacks,

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:40.440
these, like, warmed,
caramelized nuts in a bowl,

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.010
right, champagne.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:43.910
It's great, it's like a
little day off from me.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.020
No phone or anything,

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:47.050
it's like a little holiday
flying to the States, right?

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.759
I could do without the safety video.

00:00:49.759 --> 00:00:51.888
That's always a bit of a downer, right?

00:00:51.888 --> 00:00:52.721
(audience chuckling)

00:00:52.721 --> 00:00:53.770
And totally pointless,

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:57.700
if you go into the side of a
mountain at 500 miles an hour,

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:00.139
the brace position does fuck all.

00:01:00.139 --> 00:01:03.139
(audience laughing)

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:05.560
Imagine if that worked right?

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:07.290
You're going down, right, right?

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:08.917
The planes smashing, you go, I'll try it.

00:01:08.917 --> 00:01:11.230
All right, you do that, ball of flames,

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:13.370
you wake up, everyone's dead except,

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:15.270
you go, "Fucking hell, that's amazing."

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:16.176
That is...

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:19.176
(audience laughing)

00:01:22.336 --> 00:01:25.800
And they always use that voice,
don't they, on the safety,

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:28.100
they always use that voice,
that calming, hypnotic voice.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.560
Like, nothing bad happened.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:30.860
They're saying horrendous things,

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:31.900
but they're trying to make you think,

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.350
nothing bad'll happen 'cause they're,

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:35.670
I'm using this voice so
don't worry about it, right?

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:36.617
They say things, like,

00:01:36.617 --> 00:01:38.840
"In the even of the
plane landing on water,"

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:41.267
it smashes the fuck to bits, right?

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.453
(audience laughing)

00:01:42.453 --> 00:01:43.286
They say, they say,

00:01:43.286 --> 00:01:45.117
"In the event of the
plane landing on water,

00:01:45.117 --> 00:01:47.700
"your life jacket is
equipped with a whistle."

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.010
(audience laughing)

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:50.993
A fucking whistle.

00:01:50.993 --> 00:01:51.826
(audience laughing)

00:01:51.826 --> 00:01:54.450
So, the plane hits the
water, smashed into bits,

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:57.510
everyone's dead except you, by a miracle,

00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:59.900
you're bobbing around
in the Atlantic Ocean,

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:01.990
four degrees, that water is, right?

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:04.010
You've got about 15 minutes

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:05.880
before hypothermia sets in, right?

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:08.060
Or eaten by a shark, or you drown.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.189
And you're hoping they
dispatched air-sea rescue.

00:02:10.189 --> 00:02:11.022
And you're going,

00:02:11.022 --> 00:02:13.208
"Oh my God, I'm bruised, I'm
(murmurs), I'm gonna die.

00:02:13.208 --> 00:02:15.137
"I don't wanna die wet, and
I don't know what I'm doing.

00:02:15.137 --> 00:02:16.599
